"""Local Laya worker for Linux.

Speaks the same private Unix-socket protocol as the macOS Core ML worker, but
runs the pinned upstream PyTorch checkpoint (convaiinnovations/laya-multilingual)
on CUDA when available, otherwise on the CPU. The sequence construction,
temperature scaling and entropy confidence follow the upstream `laya` package
and FluidUse's LayaSequenceBuilder, so the two workers answer the same question
about the same statistics.

Usage: openzl-laya-worker prepare|start|status|stop|serve
"""

